    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and it passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when a request includes `birthDate` (ISO), return `ageBand` as `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed against `registrationDate`.\n\nI followed the repo's existing \"derived owner field\" pattern (like `locality`, `contactPreference`, `membershipLevel`) \u2014 store the input on the entity, compute the derived value in the MapStruct mapper at read time:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to `OwnerFields` (request input) and a read-only `ageBand` string to `Owner` (response). DTOs are code-generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). This was required because the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` and initializes from `schema.sql`.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `birthDate` automatically (same name on `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2192 `Owner`) and added an `ageBand(owner)` method that returns `null` when no `birthDate`/`registrationDate` is present, otherwise computes `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and bands it as MINOR/ADULT/SENIOR.\n\nThe controller already maps the incoming fields to the entity via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` and sets the effective `registrationDate`, so `birthDate` flows through with no controller change. The test creates an owner with `birthDate=1990-01-01` (registered \"today\", 2026-08-10 \u2192 age 36) and gets `ageBand=ADULT`.",
